# .audit-bin — pre-cached security scanner binaries

Pre-fetched binaries committed to the repo so the `workflow-security-audit` skill can
run without hitting the network. GitHub Actions sandboxes sometimes block outbound
connections from `run:` steps, making `pipx install` and `curl | bash` unreliable.

| File | Tool | Version | Platform |
|------|------|---------|----------|
| `zizmor` | zizmor (Trail of Bits GH Actions auditor) | v1.25.2 | linux/amd64 |
| `actionlint` | actionlint (Rhymond workflow linter) | v1.7.12 | linux/amd64 |
| `actionlint.tar.gz` | actionlint (tarball, same binary) | v1.7.12 | linux/amd64 |

The skill adds `.audit-bin/` to `PATH` before falling back to `pipx install zizmor`
or the actionlint download script.

## Updating

Replace binaries when bumping versions; also update `ZIZMOR_VERSION` in
`skills/workflow-security-audit/SKILL.md` when updating zizmor.

```bash
# zizmor — download musl binary from zizmorcore/zizmor releases
curl -L https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor/releases/download/v<VER>/zizmor-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz \
  | tar -xz zizmor && chmod +x zizmor && mv zizmor .audit-bin/

# actionlint — use the official installer, then archive it
curl -sL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rhysd/actionlint/main/scripts/download-actionlint.bash | bash
mv actionlint .audit-bin/
tar -czf .audit-bin/actionlint.tar.gz -C .audit-bin actionlint
```
